    "result_text": "All tests pass. `AcceptanceTest` is the only runnable test class (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract, `AuditLogCapture` a utility), and the full `./mvnw test` run compiled all main + test sources and reported **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (no separators), e.g. the observed `NSW2716E6609E1` = `NSW` + FY `27` + HASH8 `16E6609E` + Luhn CHK `1`.\n\n**Identity logic**\n- `CustomerCodes.java` \u2192 replaced with `MemberIds.java`: `build(owner)` now returns `region + fiscalYear2 + hash8`, then appends a single `Luhn.checkDigit(base)` over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. Dropped the removed `membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`, and `regionOf` helpers; kept `region()` and `hash8()`.\n- `AssignCustomerCode.java` \u2192 `AssignMemberId.java`: collision handling now runs against existing owners' `memberId` (appends `-<n>` on collision).\n\n**Persistence / model**\n- `Owner`: field `customerCode`/column `customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id` with `getMemberId`/`setMemberId`. Renamed the column in all four `schema.sql` files (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres).\n\n**Audit** (references memberId)\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent`: record component `customerCode` \u2192 `memberId`; `primaryIdentifier` returns `owner.getMemberId()`.\n- `AuditOwnerCreated`: human-readable line now logs `memberId=` and no longer logs the removed `membershipNumber`.\n\n**Response / API**\n- `OwnerMapper`: removed the `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` mappings and methods; `memberId` maps automatically by name (Owner\u2192DTO). `locality` now derives the region directly via `MemberIds.region(owner)` \u2014 the same REGION embedded in the memberId, which also drives `ownerSegment`.\n- `openapi.yml`: replaced `customerCode`/`checkDigit` schema with a `memberId` field and removed `membershipNumber`; the generated `OwnerDto` no longer exposes the old fields.\n- Pipeline `owners.POST.yml`: step `assignCustomerCode` \u2192 `assignMemberId`.\n\nThe `fiscalYear` field remains (derived from `registrationDate`) and is consistent with the FY segment now embedded in `memberId`.",
